thmonoidsig ≔ (lines "infixl 7 ⋆ mop A\ninfixl 7 mop mop A\nconst 0 ε munit\nconst 0 munit munit")
thmonoidrules ∶ (𝔏 𝕊)
thmonoidrules ≔ (lines "mop(x, munit) ==> x\nmop(munit, x) ==> x")
thmonoidaxioms ∶ (𝔏 𝕊)
thmonoidaxioms ≔ (lines "a monoid is a set with an associative operation ⋆ and a neutral element ε:\nM1 (x ⋆ y) ⋆ z = x ⋆ (y ⋆ z)\nM2 x ⋆ ε = x\nM3 ε ⋆ x = x\nnothing else is assumed: the operation need not be commutative (the words are free monoid words), and there is no cancellation: x ⋆ y = x ⋆ z does not give y = z; the package group adds inverses")
thmonoidtheorems ∶ (𝔏 𝕊)
thmonoidtheorems ≔ (lines "(x ⋆ y) ⋆ z = x ⋆ (y ⋆ z)\nx ⋆ ε = x\nε ⋆ x = x\nε ⋆ ε = ε\nx ⋆ ε ⋆ y = x ⋆ y\nx ⋆ y ⋆ z ⋆ w = (x ⋆ y) ⋆ (z ⋆ w)\n(x ⋆ y) ⋆ ε = x ⋆ y\nx ⋆ (ε ⋆ y ⋆ ε) = x ⋆ y\nx ⋆ y = y ⋆ x <=> x ⋆ y = y ⋆ x\nx ⋆ x ⋆ x = x ⋆ (x ⋆ x)")
thmonoiddoc ∶ 𝕊
thmonoiddoc ≔ "monoids: an associative operation with a neutral element, the words of the free monoid; no commutativity and no cancellation"
thmonoid ∶ Theory
thmonoid ≔ (mktheory "monoid" (∷ "core" ⊘) (∷ "cmonoid" ⊘) ⊥ thmonoidsig thmonoidrules ⊘ thmonoidaxioms thmonoidtheorems thmonoiddoc)
